{"name":"Spring Onion","hex":"#596c3c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring onion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young plant of Allium sp. (typically Welsh onion, onion, or shallot) with tender edible leaves and an undeveloped bulb."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring_onion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Scallion","blocks":[{"text":"Scallions are edible vegetables of various species in the genus Allium. Scallions generally have a milder taste than most onions. Green onions/scallions have a long, delicate green stem that is white near the root. They have no bulb and a mild, sweet onion flavour. Their close relatives include garlic, shallots, leeks, chives, and Chinese onions. The leaves are eaten both raw and cooked."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/CSA-Red-Spring-Onions.jpg/330px-CSA-Red-Spring-Onions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scallion","wikidata":"Q774278"},{"title":"Onion","blocks":[{"text":"The onion, also known as the bulb onion or common onion, is a vegetable that is the most widely cultivated species of the genus Allium. The shallot is a botanical variety of the onion which was classified as a separate species until 2011. The onion's close relatives include garlic, scallion, leek, and chives."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Mixed_onions.jpg/330px-Mixed_onions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onion","wikidata":"Q23485"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Germinating_scallion.jpg/500px-Germinating_scallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Germinating_scallion.jpg/500px-Germinating_scallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm